    ],
    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Imagine walking up to the door of a club and being stopped by a robot guard called “Humanity”. It "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "squints",
            "zh": "眯眼"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " its camera eyes and says, “Prove you’re not AI. One word.” You might try something impressive like "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "photosynthesis",
            "zh": "光合作用"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", but honestly, the best answer is much simpler—and far less confident: "
          },
          {
            "t": "em",
            "v": "Um"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Not a loud “UM” that you’re "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "yelling",
            "zh": "叫喊"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " at your mum from the other room. Just a soft “um”—the sound your brain makes when it "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "trips over",
            "zh": "绊倒"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " its own shoelaces. “Um” is like a tiny, "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "verbal",
            "zh": "口头的"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "shrug",
            "zh": "耸肩"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". It happens when your thoughts arrive late to a meeting, and you need a second to catch up. "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Linguists",
            "zh": "语言学家"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " call it a "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "filled pause",
            "zh": "填声停顿"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". It helps humans plan what to say, take turns in conversation, and correct themselves in real time."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "That’s why “um” is such a perfect human password. Humans don’t run "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "smoothly",
            "ref": "v-smoothly"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". We pause. We hesitate. Sometimes, we even restart a sentence halfway through, like a laptop with too many "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "tabs",
            "zh": "标签页"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " open. And unlike a machine, our hesitation isn’t just a delay; it often carries feeling."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Sometimes “um” is funny. It’s the sound you make when you forget what you were saying but try to play it cool. But sometimes it’s heavier. “Um” can show up when you’re nervous, embarrassed, or trying to say something important. It can show fear, tightening your throat, or kindness, searching for the right words so that you don’t hurt someone."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "That’s the real difference between AI and humanity: We are messy in a strangely beautiful way. We feel strong emotions—joy, guilt, love, jealousy, hope—sometimes all before breakfast. We care, even when it’s inconvenient. We love people who "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "annoy",
            "ref": "v-annoy"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " us. We forgive, even when it’s hard. We get things wrong and then try again. We apologise badly. We cry at movies about talking dogs. We laugh at jokes that aren’t even that funny."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Under all that "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "chaos",
            "zh": "杂乱"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " is something real: a "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "clumsy",
            "zh": "笨拙的"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " yet "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "stubborn",
            "ref": "v-stubborn"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " care for others. It’s not efficient or perfectly "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "logical",
            "ref": "v-logical"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". But it is deeply, unmistakably human."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p7",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Could an "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "algorithm",
            "zh": "算法"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " generate the word “um”? Sure, but could it "
          },
          {
            "t": "em",
            "v": "mean"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " it? Could it experience the awkward heat of a "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "blush",
            "zh": "脸红"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " or the painful courage it takes to say “I’m sorry”?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p8",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Um... probably not."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
